{"name":"Cloak of Mystery","hex":"#916660","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cloak","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A long outer garment worn over the shoulders covering the back; a cape, often with a hood.","A blanket-like covering, often metaphorical."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover as with or like a cloak.","To cover up, hide or conceal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cloak"},{"term":"mystery","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Something secret or unexplainable; an unknown.","Someone or something with an obscure or puzzling nature."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mystery"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cloak of Mystery","blocks":[{"text":"Cloak of Mystery is an American anthology television series. It was broadcast by NBC, recycling programs originally telecast on The Alcoa Theatre and The General Electric Theater."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cloak_of_Mystery"},{"title":"Cloak","blocks":[{"text":"A cloak is a type of loose garment worn over clothing, mostly but not always, as outerwear for outdoor wear, which serves the same purpose as an overcoat and protects the wearer from the weather. It may form part of a uniform. People in many different societies may wear cloaks. Over time, cloak designs have changed to match fashion and available textiles."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Fashion_Plate_Manteau_1823.jpg/330px-Fashion_Plate_Manteau_1823.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cloak"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Cloak.jpg/500px-Cloak.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Cloak.jpg/500px-Cloak.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cloak, 1580–1600 Victoria an